rknpu (0.9.8-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Support validated combined-mask dual/triple-core submits with common task
    IOVA and per-core task ranges; retain deterministic single-core AUTO.
  * Validate the official classification/detection/dynamic-shape/MatMul matrix,
    ALL mask, sync/async output fences, and mindnano inference.
  * Account NPU busy time per section completion so debugfs/rknpu/load reports
    short-burst utilization instead of staying at 0%.
  * Reset stale runtime PM state so RKNPU ioctls do not fail after unbinding the
    in-tree rocket driver.
  * Remove the per-file task-token fastpath that could dereference a recycled
    GEM handle across rknn_matmul contexts.
  * Validate populated subcore_task ranges instead of the top-level task sum for
    large multi-core submits.

 -- lurenJBD <31967654+lurenJBD@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 25 Sep 2026 22:16:34 +0800

rknpu (0.9.8-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Implement submit fastpaths (zero-alloc sync args, IOMMU detach early exit, task token hot-cache).
  * Add dynamic multi-core dispatch AUTO mask preservation and subcore_task scheduling.
  * Performance release: MobileNet v1 peak 322.8 FPS, MatMul 11.2k ops/s.

 -- lurenJBD <31967654+lurenJBD@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 16:15:00 +0800

rknpu (0.9.8-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release of mainline Rockchip RK3588 RKNPU DKMS driver package.
  * Target mainline device tree compatible: rockchip,rk3588-rknn-core.
  * 3-core NPU concurrency and dynamic devfreq OPP (200-800 MHz).
  * IOMMU per-domain accounting and pool isolation supporting 4+ GiB LLM models.
  * Native PC engine with PC_DMA_BASE=0 protocol.
  * Non-blocking async submit and dma_fence integration.

 -- lurenJBD <31967654+lurenJBD@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 13:30:00 +0800
